# A study note written entirely in flow mode: no coordinates needed.
document size=a4 layout=pages pattern=dots
defaults size=16

h1 "The Krebs Cycle" rule
para "The citric acid cycle oxidizes **acetyl-CoA** to CO₂ and captures the energy as *NADH*, *FADH₂* and GTP. It runs in the **mitochondrial matrix**."

h2 "Key facts"
bullet "Takes place twice per glucose molecule"
bullet "Each turn produces 3 NADH, 1 FADH₂ and 1 GTP"
bullet "Oxaloacetate is regenerated at the end"
bullet "it's a cycle, not a pathway" level=2

h2 "Overview"
mermaid
flowchart TD
  G[Glycolysis] -->|2 pyruvate| K(Krebs cycle)
  K -->|3 NADH, 1 FADH2| E(Electron transport chain)
  K -->|1 GTP| ATP((ATP))
  E -->|~34 ATP| ATP
  K -->|2 CO2| X[Exhaled]
end

h2 "Yield per turn"
table
| Product | Count | Where it goes |
|---------|:-----:|---------------|
| NADH    | 3     | Electron transport chain |
| FADH₂   | 1     | Electron transport chain |
| GTP     | 1     | Converted to ATP |
| CO₂     | 2     | Exhaled |
end

callout "Mnemonic: **C**an **I** **K**eep **S**elling **S**ex **F**or **M**oney, **O**fficer?" title="Remember the order"

h2 "To review"
